{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And it shall be on the seventh day that he shall shave all his hair.</b> And afterward it specifies: <b>his head and his beard and his eyebrows.</b> Even though our Sages of blessed memory (Sotah 16a) interpreted this by the hermeneutical rule of general and particular — yet according to our way we may say that it specified these three principal limbs because they are close to the three principal transgressions on account of which afflictions come. <b>His head</b> — to atone for arrogance, which desires to be the head over everything, as it is written (Isaiah 3:16-17): ״יַעַן כִּי גָבְהוּ בְּנוֹת צִיּוֹן וְגוֹ׳ וְשִׂפַּח ה׳ קָדְקֹד בְּנוֹת צִיּוֹן״ ('Because the daughters of Zion are haughty… and HaShem will smite the crown of the head of the daughters of Zion'). <b>And his beard</b> — these are the hairs around his mouth, to atone for the mouth that speaks lashon ha-ra. <b>And his eyebrows</b> — to atone for narrowness of eye."], :book :leviticus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The abbreviation ה׳ in the Isaiah quotation is expanded as HaShem per the voice rules for reverent abbreviations of divine names."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:36:33.474834222Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}